\contentsline {table}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Origin of each grid value used in Fig.~\ref {fig:Factorization_ratios_Pb034_eta8_PL-1}. ``Quad.\ $(b_1^2, b_2^2, b_3^2)$'' means the parabola in $b^2$ through the data at those three points on the same $P\cdot b$ row; ``lin.\ $[b_a^2, b_b^2]$'' means linear interpolation in $b^2$ between the data at $b_a^2$ and $b_b^2$. Where a cell has two entries, the upper one gives the linear points (circles) and the lower one the quadratic points (triangles) of Fig.~\ref {fig:Factorization_ratios_Pb034_eta8_PL-1}. The pattern is the same for all three amplitudes.\relax }}{124}{table.caption.79}%
